hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"572","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""There is a surah in the Qur'an of thirty verses, it interceded for its reciter until he was forgiven; that surah is Surah Al-Mulk."
"573","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People! Gather together."" Then he (peace be upon him) came to us and said: ""I will recite to you one third of the Qur'an."" Then he (peace be upon him) recited Surah Al-Ikhlas until he completed it and did not add anything to it. Someone said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon I will recite to you one third of the Qur'an."" He did not add anything to it, and this is news from the heavens. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us and said: ""I told you that soon I would recite to you one third of the Qur'an, because Surah Al-Ikhlas is equal to one third of the Qur'an."
"574","With this same chain: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The house most devoid of goodness is the one that is devoid of the Book of Allah."
"575","With this chain of narration, it is reported from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him: He said, ""Whoever swears an oath by a surah of the Qur'an, then if he is wicked, for every verse of it there is an oath of patience upon him."
"576","With this same chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every Muslim is forbidden to another Muslim. By the One in Whose hand is my soul! Satan leaves the house in which he hears the recitation of Surah Al-Baqarah."" And he said: ""Patience is from Allah, and haste is from Satan."
